## 7. Assumptions & Limitations

- StatsBomb coordinates are precise to ~0.1 pitch units (~8cm) — sufficient for displacement measurement but not perfect
- The data cannot distinguish whether displacement was intentional (tactical) or unchallenged by the referee
- Tournament samples are smaller than league datasets, limiting generalizability
- xT is a static grid model and does not account for player positioning at the moment of the throw

